# The Poké Radar on Route 222's grass (decomp pokeradar.c RefreshRadarChain, RadarChargeStep): Y with the Radar
# registered and the battery flat runs POKE_RADAR 0 (50 steps left); fifty steps charge it, out of the grass and back;
# Y again empties the battery and the patches shake.
# Setup: Repel steps (no ordinary encounter on the way), Master Balls for the chain, and the registered Radar.
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_GARCHOMP 50 platinum:MOVE_DRAGON_CLAW
give item platinum:ITEM_POKE_RADAR 1
give item platinum:ITEM_MASTER_BALL 12
set state repel 250
set state registeredItem "platinum:ITEM_POKE_RADAR"
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_222 750 777 right
until idle
+0 press y
+1 release y
until message
advance text
until idle
+0 assert state encounters.radarCharge 0
+0 press right
until position 770 777
+0 release right
until idle
+0 press down
until position 770 778
+0 release down
until idle
+0 press left
until position 741 778
+0 release left
until idle
+0 press right
until position 744 778
+0 release right
until idle
+0 assert state encounters.radarCharge 50
+0 press y
+1 release y
+20 screenshot radar-patches
until idle
+0 assert state encounters.radarCharge 0
